<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50459" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ventōsĭtas</span></b> ,
			ātis, f.
		ventosus (postclass.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>windiness</i>, <i>flatulence</i>, <i>ventosity</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ventris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
					Aur. Tard. 4, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stomachi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Herb. 126</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>a puffing up</i>,
				<i>inflation</i>, <i>conceit</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Fulg. Myth. 2, 17</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
